        "body": "The Bots panel issued two requests per bot every five seconds, including quota reads that lock bot rows. Runtime also rerendered the entire table every second, and overlapping refreshes could race with session-preview changes.\n\nThis adds a read-only, single-statement activity snapshot and reuses the existing runtime snapshot, reducing recurring Bots activity/runtime requests to two per refresh. Polling is serialized, pauses and aborts reads while hidden, and resumes on return. Manual refreshes after preview changes wait for a fresh request. Per-bot pending state protects Show/Hide controls when several bots are updated. Only blocked runtime rows need the one-second clock.\n\nThe snapshot retains the existing counters, 0–25 display limit, durable request deduplication, original reservation-day accounting, and conservative persisted usage. The authoritative offer quota guard, session files, browser lifecycle and database schema are unchanged by the new performance commit.\n\nBranch context: GitHub records PR #227 merged at 34df72d, but stable currently points to its older ancestor 8d869b2. This branch descends from 34df72d and therefore also includes the previously requested changes from #222–#227: capacity-aware scheduling, session preview, exact category matching, separate backoffs and service-worker default. Preserve the current stable ref before merging; do not force-push it.\n\nValidation: five deterministic polling tests, TypeScript/Vite production build and ESLint pass locally (one pre-existing unrelated hook warning). PostgreSQL integration tests cover snapshot parity, deduplication, midnight boundaries, ownership checks and read-only behavior. Full Backend / Frontend / Mobile / Playwright unit CI must pass before merge. The existing bundle workflow must complete after merge so the panel served by Spring Boot is also updated.\n\nClosed without merging after retrieving the user's newer rollback instructions. Stable was intentionally restored to PR #221, and the user excluded reinstating scheduler/category/offer changes. Preserve this experimental performance branch; implement only session-preview controls on top of 8d869b2 in a separate PR.",
